<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Theoretical Appendices</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Algorithm Pipeline of DiEP</h3>

<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span><span id="alg1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DiEP</span> – Differentiable Expert Pruning</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.6.1" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="alg1.6.1.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="alg1.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> </span>Model inputs <math id="alg1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{x}</annotation></semantics></math>, targets <math id="alg1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒚</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{y}</annotation></semantics></math>, initial intra-layer scores <math id="alg1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha^{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, initial inter-layer scores <math id="alg1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta^{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, regularization coefficient <math id="alg1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>.
</div>
<div id="alg1.6.2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="alg1.6.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span> <em id="alg1.6.2.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">not converged</em> <span id="alg1.6.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.6.3" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="alg1.6.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">/* </span><span id="alg1.6.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Update intra-layer scores (fix <math id="alg1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>)  */</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.6.4" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> Update <math id="alg1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha^{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha^{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math> by descending:

<table id="A2.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\alpha}\big(\mathcal{L}_{ce}(\boldsymbol{y},\mathcal{F}^{\prime}(\boldsymbol{x};\alpha^{t},\beta^{t}))+\lambda\Phi(\alpha^{t},\beta^{t})\big)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>α</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\alpha}\big(\mathcal{L}_{ce}(\boldsymbol{y},\mathcal{F}^{\prime}(\boldsymbol{x};\alpha^{t},\beta^{t}))+\lambda\Phi(\alpha^{t},\beta^{t})\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="alg1.6.5" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="alg1.6.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">/* </span><span id="alg1.6.5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Update inter-layer scores (fix <math id="alg1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>)  */</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.6.6" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> Update <math id="alg1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta^{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta^{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math> by descending:

<table id="A2.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\beta}\big(\mathcal{L}_{ce}(\boldsymbol{y},\mathcal{F}^{\prime}(\boldsymbol{x};\alpha^{t+1},\beta^{t}))+\lambda\Phi(\alpha^{t+1},\beta^{t})\big)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>β</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\beta}\big(\mathcal{L}_{ce}(\boldsymbol{y},\mathcal{F}^{\prime}(\boldsymbol{x};\alpha^{t+1},\beta^{t}))+\lambda\Phi(\alpha^{t+1},\beta^{t})\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>Set <math id="alg1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leftarrow t+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leftarrow t+1</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.6.7" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="alg1.6.7.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="alg1.6.7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> </span>Optimized intra-layer importance scores <math id="alg1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> and inter-layer importance scores <math id="alg1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>.
</div>
<div id="alg1.6.8" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Convergence Analysis of DiEP</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta\coloneqq\{(\alpha,\beta)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta\coloneqq\{(\alpha,\beta)\}</annotation></semantics></math> be the parameter space, where
<math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\mathbb{R}^{NL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\mathbb{R}^{NL}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\in\mathbb{R}^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>L</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\in\mathbb{R}^{L}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Denote <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{1}\!=\!\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{1}\!=\!\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{2}\!=\!\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{2}\!=\!\beta</annotation></semantics></math>.
The overall objective of <span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DiEP</span> is</p>
<table id="A2.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}(\theta_{1},\theta_{2})\;=\;\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{ce}}\bigl(\mathbf{y},\mathcal{F}^{\prime}(\mathbf{x};\theta_{1},\theta_{2})\bigr)\;+\;\lambda\,\bigl\lVert\mathcal{F}^{\prime}(\mathbf{x};\theta_{1},\theta_{2})-\mathcal{F}(\mathbf{x})\bigr\rVert_{F}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>ce</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(\theta_{1},\theta_{2})\;=\;\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{ce}}\bigl(\mathbf{y},\mathcal{F}^{\prime}(\mathbf{x};\theta_{1},\theta_{2})\bigr)\;+\;\lambda\,\bigl\lVert\mathcal{F}^{\prime}(\mathbf{x};\theta_{1},\theta_{2})-\mathcal{F}(\mathbf{x})\bigr\rVert_{F}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Assumptions.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:20pt;">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A2.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">A1</span>.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Lower<span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>Boundedness.</span>
<math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\inf_{(\alpha,\beta)\in\Theta}\mathcal{L}(\alpha,\beta)\;&gt;\;-\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">inf</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">&gt;</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\inf_{(\alpha,\beta)\in\Theta}\mathcal{L}(\alpha,\beta)\;&gt;\;-\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A2.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">A2</span>.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Lipschitz Smoothness.</span>
<math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta_{i}}\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta_{i}}\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text">-</span>Lipschitz continuous,
i.e. <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\nabla_{\theta_{i}}\mathcal{L}(u)-\nabla_{\theta_{i}}\mathcal{L}(v)\rVert\leq L_{i}\lVert u-v\rVert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\nabla_{\theta_{i}}\mathcal{L}(u)-\nabla_{\theta_{i}}\mathcal{L}(v)\rVert\leq L_{i}\lVert u-v\rVert</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,2\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,2\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A2.I1.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">A3</span>.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Stepsizes.</span> Fixed learning rates satisfy
<math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 0&lt;\eta_{i}&lt;\tfrac{2}{L_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 0&lt;\eta_{i}&lt;\tfrac{2}{L_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,2\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,2\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A2.I1.i4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">A4</span>.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Level<span id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>Set Boundedness.</span>
The set <math id="A2.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(\alpha,\beta)\in\Theta:\mathcal{L}(\alpha,\beta)\leq\mathcal{L}(\alpha^{0},\beta^{0})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(\alpha,\beta)\in\Theta:\mathcal{L}(\alpha,\beta)\leq\mathcal{L}(\alpha^{0},\beta^{0})\}</annotation></semantics></math>
is compact.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Algorithmic update.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0,1,\dots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0,1,\dots</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A2.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\theta_{i}^{\,t+1}\;=\;\theta_{i}^{\,t}-\eta_{i}\,\nabla_{\theta_{i}}\mathcal{L}(\theta_{1}^{\,t},\theta_{2}^{\,t}),\quad i\in\{1,2\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\theta_{i}^{\,t+1}\;=\;\theta_{i}^{\,t}-\eta_{i}\,\nabla_{\theta_{i}}\mathcal{L}(\theta_{1}^{\,t},\theta_{2}^{\,t}),\quad i\in\{1,2\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1</span></span><span id="Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Descent)<span id="Thmlemma1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under <span id="Thmlemma1.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">A2</span>–<span id="Thmlemma1.p1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">A3</span>,
<math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}(\theta_{1}^{\,t+1},\theta_{2}^{\,t+1})\;\leq\;\mathcal{L}(\theta_{1}^{\,t},\theta_{2}^{\,t})-\sum_{i=1}^{2}\frac{(2-\eta_{i}L_{i})}{2\eta_{i}}\bigl\lVert\theta_{i}^{\,t+1}-\theta_{i}^{\,t}\bigr\rVert^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><msup><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(\theta_{1}^{\,t+1},\theta_{2}^{\,t+1})\;\leq\;\mathcal{L}(\theta_{1}^{\,t},\theta_{2}^{\,t})-\sum_{i=1}^{2}\frac{(2-\eta_{i}L_{i})}{2\eta_{i}}\bigl\lVert\theta_{i}^{\,t+1}-\theta_{i}^{\,t}\bigr\rVert^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Apply the standard descent lemma to each block update in (<a href="#A2.E13" title="In Algorithmic update. ‣ B.2 Convergence Analysis of DiEP ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Appendices ‣ DiEP: Adaptive Mixture-of-Experts Compression through Differentiable Expert Pruning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmcorollary1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmcorollary1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 1</span></span><span id="Thmcorollary1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Monotonicity and Bounded Iterates)<span id="Thmcorollary1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmcorollary1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmcorollary1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmcorollary1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assumptions <span id="Thmcorollary1.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">A1</span>–<span id="Thmcorollary1.p1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">A4</span> imply
<math id="Thmcorollary1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl\{\mathcal{L}(\theta_{1}^{\,t},\theta_{2}^{\,t})\bigr\}_{t\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl\{\mathcal{L}(\theta_{1}^{\,t},\theta_{2}^{\,t})\bigr\}_{t\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math>
is monotonically non<span id="Thmcorollary1.p1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text">-</span>increasing and convergent,
and
<math id="Thmcorollary1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(\theta_{1}^{\,t},\theta_{2}^{\,t})\}_{t\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(\theta_{1}^{\,t},\theta_{2}^{\,t})\}_{t\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2</span></span><span id="Thmlemma2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Vanishing Updates)<span id="Thmlemma2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\lim_{t\to\infty}\bigl\lVert\theta_{i}^{\,t+1}-\theta_{i}^{\,t}\bigr\rVert=0,\;i\in\{1,2\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em">=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lim_{t\to\infty}\bigl\lVert\theta_{i}^{\,t+1}-\theta_{i}^{\,t}\bigr\rVert=0,\;i\in\{1,2\}.</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Summing the non<span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>negative terms in Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Descent). ‣ Algorithmic update. ‣ B.2 Convergence Analysis of DiEP ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Appendices ‣ DiEP: Adaptive Mixture-of-Experts Compression through Differentiable Expert Pruning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> over <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>
gives a telescoping series dominated by
<math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(\theta_{1}^{\,0},\theta_{2}^{\,0})-\inf\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn> 0</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn> 0</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(\theta_{1}^{\,0},\theta_{2}^{\,0})-\inf\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math>; hence the series of squared update norms is finite.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Subsequence Convergence to Critical Points)<span id="Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under <span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">A1</span>–<span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">A4</span>,
the sequence <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(\theta_{1}^{\,t},\theta_{2}^{\,t})\}_{t\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(\theta_{1}^{\,t},\theta_{2}^{\,t})\}_{t\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math>
generated by (<a href="#A2.E13" title="In Algorithmic update. ‣ B.2 Convergence Analysis of DiEP ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Appendices ‣ DiEP: Adaptive Mixture-of-Experts Compression through Differentiable Expert Pruning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>)
possesses at least one convergent subsequence,
and <em id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">every</em> limit point <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\theta_{1}^{\star},\theta_{2}^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\theta_{1}^{\star},\theta_{2}^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math>
satisfies
<math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta_{1}}\mathcal{L}(\theta_{1}^{\star},\theta_{2}^{\star})=\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta_{1}}\mathcal{L}(\theta_{1}^{\star},\theta_{2}^{\star})=\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta_{2}}\mathcal{L}(\theta_{1}^{\star},\theta_{2}^{\star})=\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta_{2}}\mathcal{L}(\theta_{1}^{\star},\theta_{2}^{\star})=\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math>;
i.e. it is a critical point of <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Corollary <a href="#Thmcorollary1" title="Corollary 1 (Monotonicity and Bounded Iterates). ‣ Algorithmic update. ‣ B.2 Convergence Analysis of DiEP ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Appendices ‣ DiEP: Adaptive Mixture-of-Experts Compression through Differentiable Expert Pruning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and <span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">A4</span>,
<math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(\theta_{1}^{\,t},\theta_{2}^{\,t})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(\theta_{1}^{\,t},\theta_{2}^{\,t})\}</annotation></semantics></math> lies in a compact set; hence
the Bolzano–Weierstrass theorem guarantees a convergent subsequence
<math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\theta_{1}^{\,t_{k}},\theta_{2}^{\,t_{k}})\to(\theta_{1}^{\star},\theta_{2}^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\theta_{1}^{\,t_{k}},\theta_{2}^{\,t_{k}})\to(\theta_{1}^{\star},\theta_{2}^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2 (Vanishing Updates). ‣ Algorithmic update. ‣ B.2 Convergence Analysis of DiEP ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Appendices ‣ DiEP: Adaptive Mixture-of-Experts Compression through Differentiable Expert Pruning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> gives <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{i}^{\,t_{k}+1}-\theta_{i}^{\,t_{k}}\to\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{i}^{\,t_{k}+1}-\theta_{i}^{\,t_{k}}\to\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Dividing (<a href="#A2.E13" title="In Algorithmic update. ‣ B.2 Convergence Analysis of DiEP ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Appendices ‣ DiEP: Adaptive Mixture-of-Experts Compression through Differentiable Expert Pruning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>) by <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and taking <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\!\to\!\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\!\to\!\infty</annotation></semantics></math> yields
<math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta_{i}}\mathcal{L}(\theta_{1}^{\star},\theta_{2}^{\star})=\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta_{i}}\mathcal{L}(\theta_{1}^{\star},\theta_{2}^{\star})=\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,2</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Discussion.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Subsequence Convergence to Critical Points). ‣ Algorithmic update. ‣ B.2 Convergence Analysis of DiEP ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Appendices ‣ DiEP: Adaptive Mixture-of-Experts Compression through Differentiable Expert Pruning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> aligns with the classical results of
block coordinate descent <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>)</cite> while instantiating them
for our two<span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>block differentiable pruning objective.
It guarantees that <span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">DiEP</span> converges (up to subsequences)
to first<span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text">-</span>order stationary points under standard smoothness and stepsize conditions.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Limitations</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">While our proposed DiEP method achieves strong performance in MoE pruning, several limitations remain. Due to computational constraints, our main experiments cannot be conducted on some larger-scale MoE models, like Deepseek V3 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>]</cite>, and Qwen2.5-Max <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">42</a>]</cite>. Furthermore, our study primarily focuses on language models, leaving the effectiveness of DiEP in multimodal MoE architectures unexplored. Investigating whether our approach can achieve competitive performance on Vision-Language tasks, such as MoE-LLaVA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>]</cite>, remains an important direction for future research.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Broader impacts</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The development of DiEP, a method for compressing large Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) models, carries several potential societal impacts, both positive and negative. Positive impacts: In regions or scenarios where access to high-performance computing infrastructure is limited, DiEP can enable the deployment of capable AI models that would otherwise be infeasible. This could support applications in education, healthcare, and public services in underserved communities. Negative impacts: As AI models become more capable and efficient, they may automate tasks currently performed by humans, potentially leading to job displacement in certain sectors. While DiEP aims at efficiency, the broader trend of AI advancement contributes to this concern.</p>
</div>
</section>
</article>
</div>
</div>
